## Model card

- **Name:** Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite
- **Short description:** Google’s Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite is a low-cost, low-latency multimodal model for high-volume classification, extraction, and lightweight tasks with 1M-token input context.
- **Provider / access:** Google AI Studio / Gemini API. Local metadata lists `google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite`, paid $0.10/$0.40 per 1M, and `noFreeId` on OpenCode Zen.
- **Release / knowledge:** Google AI developer docs reviewed 2026-11-10 (latest update July 2025). Knowledge cutoff: January 2025 (per docs).
- **IDs:** `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`, `Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite`.
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 input tokens; 65,536 output tokens (Google docs).
- **Modalities:** Text, image, video, audio, and PDF input; text output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** Paid $0.10/$0.40 per 1M in/out; free tier available on Google AI Studio with standard rate limits (local metadata/docs context).
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Google multimodal model. Architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

